{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D#m]The third seal, a black horse, its rider is Death
And Hades follows close behind
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[B]The [D#m]Lamb has opened the first seal
A voice like thunder cries out, come
A white horse rides, its [B]rider holds a bow
[C#]He [D#m]goes out conquering, a crown upon his head
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
The second seal, a fiery red horse
Its rid[B]er [D#m]takes the peace from the earth
A great sword in his hand
And peo[B]ple turn on [C#]one an[D#m]oth[F#]er
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Come, cries [C#]the thunder
The horsemen [D#m]ride [F#][C#]
Who [D#m]can stand [F#]before the [C#]Lamb
When the seals are opened [B]wide
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [B] | [C#] | [C#] | [D#m] |
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] |
| [D#m] | [B] | [C#] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D#m]The third seal, a black horse
A pair of scales in its rider's [B]hand [C#]
[D#m]The fourth, a pale horse, its rider is Death
And Hades follows close be[B]hind [C#]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D#m]Come, [F#]cries the [C#]thunder
The horsemen [D#m]ride [F#][C#]
Who [D#m]can stand [F#]before the [C#]Lamb
When the seals are opened [B]wide
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
